From 69d09bdf99f3837c7d8eccbd7440e262ba22d276 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable entries in Settings, Display and App
 info

KEYBOARD_FIRST_SETTINGS_UX and APP_DISPLAY_COMPATIBILITY_PROFILES_UX
entry points into the Sable apps that own these settings. Settings only
opens them; the settings stay in their apps.

* Settings > Sable (homepage row after System): Sable Start (home
  layout), Quick bar (Sable Start's editor, action
  org.sableos.start.action.EDIT_QUICK_BAR), Sable Hub, Diagnostics
  (Sable Tools), Hardware tests (Sable Tools OPEN_TOOL HARDWARE_TESTS)
  and App display compatibility.
* Settings > Display > App display compatibility.
* App info > Display compatibility opens that app's profile
  (org.sableos.titan2.displaycompat.action.APP_PROFILE with a package:
  URI); launcher apps of the current user only.

Every link resolves to an explicit component in its owner's package,
so a row is hidden when its app is absent, and the homepage row when
all are. The Sable page is search-indexed with keywords (display
compat, quick bar, diagnostics, factory test, ...); rows of absent apps
are non-indexable and the page is left out of search when no owner is
installed. The page gets the Sable list keyboard (type-ahead, /
search, Home/End).
